% review-id: sambalele
% review-from: holding
% review-status: pending
% review-categories: violence, racism, sexual
% review-findings: Verse I: "Sambalele precisava e dumas boas lambadas" (Sambalele needed a good thrashing). The chorus sings "mulata" four times ("Pisa, pisa, pisa, mulata ... na barra da saia, mulata"), a word for a mixed-race woman with a colonial and racial history; verses II and III court a "mulata bonita" (how does one court? where do you live?).
% review-suggestion: Keep it out of the published set until a Brazilian educator gives the words classes sing today. Choosing other verses is not enough, because "mulata" is in the chorus; do not invent replacement words here.
